.TH CVECTOR_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_reset \- clear all elements and reset capacity
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

void cvector_reset(cvec v);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes every element from the vector and then tries to shrink the
capacity back to the minimum of 4 elements. If that reallocation fails the
capacity stays as it was, but the element count becomes 0 anyway.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to reset
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The element count becomes 0, and the capacity goes back to the minimum
(4) when the reallocation succeeds.

The elements are not freed one by one; the caller has to do that first
when it is needed. Asserts if v is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_reset (3),
.BR cvector_destroy (3)
